// kdk-lab unattended-upgrades policy for the three Raspberry Pi 5 hosts
// (kdk-mon-01, kdk-dkr-02, kdk-dkr-03; Raspberry Pi OS = Debian 13 + the
// Raspberry Pi Foundation archive). Install as
// /etc/apt/apt.conf.d/52kdk-unattended-upgrades (root:root 0644).
// Source of truth: hosts/_common/apt/ in BigH3ater/kdk-lab-dkr.
//
// Why a drop-in and why #clear: see 52kdk-unattended-upgrades (the VM file).
// The Raspberry Pi Foundation origin carries the kernel, firmware, and the
// +rpt rebuilds of libc6/libssl3 -- without it those never auto-apply
// (hosts report H-01: 64 pending on every Pi).
//
// Docker CE restarts dockerd on upgrade: install only after daemon.json has
// "live-restore": true on the host.
// Automatic reboot at 04:30 when a package asks for one (kernel/firmware/libc).
// kdk-dkr-03 runs NUT: a reboot restarts the nut-upsd container, which is
// fine while NUT is read-only (no upsmon clients); revisit if that changes.
#clear Unattended-Upgrade::Origins-Pattern;
Unattended-Upgrade::Origins-Pattern {
        "origin=Debian,codename=${distro_codename},label=Debian";
        "origin=Debian,codename=${distro_codename},label=Debian-Security";
        "origin=Debian,codename=${distro_codename}-security,label=Debian-Security";
        "origin=Raspberry Pi Foundation,codename=${distro_codename}";
        "origin=Docker,codename=${distro_codename},label=Docker CE";
};
Unattended-Upgrade::Remove-Unused-Kernel-Packages "true";
Unattended-Upgrade::Automatic-Reboot "true";
Unattended-Upgrade::Automatic-Reboot-WithUsers "true";
Unattended-Upgrade::Automatic-Reboot-Time "04:30";
